Common Prompt: 
You are a senior full-stack engineer and UI/UX designer. Build the complete front-end interface (a fully clickable, professional prototype) for a web platform called "BAUST Career Bridge".

=== 1. PROJECT CONTEXT ===
Bangladesh Army University of Science and Technology (BAUST) has no central digital platform connecting current students with alumni. Problems:
- No structured mentorship (career planning, higher studies, CV review, interview prep).
- No central alumni database, so students cannot find alumni working in govt, private, multinational, research or business sectors.
- No profile verification, so fake profiles are common on social media.
- Alumni have no digital channel to request transcripts, certificates or official documents from the university.

BAUST Career Bridge is a web and mobile-responsive platform connecting Alumni, Current Students and University Administration. It is not just a chat app; it is a complete Career Support & Administrative Network System.

=== 2. TECH STACK ===
- React + TypeScript + Vite
- Tailwind CSS
- React Router (multi-page navigation)
- lucide-react for icons
- recharts for charts
- Use realistic MOCK DATA only (no backend). Keep all mock data in /src/data/ as separate files.
- Use localStorage to persist demo state (login role, requests, messages).

=== 3. DESIGN SYSTEM (strictly follow) ===
- Style: clean, modern, trustworthy, university/corporate look. Not childish.
- Primary: deep navy (#0F2A4A). Secondary: army green (#2E5E3E). Accent: gold (#C9A227). Background: soft gray (#F5F7FA). Cards: white, rounded-2xl, soft shadow.
- Font: "Inter" for English and "Noto Sans Bengali" for Bangla text.
- Consistent spacing, 8px grid, clear typography hierarchy.
- Fully responsive (mobile, tablet, desktop). Sidebar on desktop, bottom nav or hamburger on mobile.
- Include loading skeletons, empty states, hover and focus states, and smooth subtle transitions.
- Status badges with colors: Pending (amber), Approved (green), Rejected (red), In Progress (blue).
- Add a simple language toggle (EN / বাংলা) in the navbar for the main UI labels.

=== 4. USER ROLES ===
1. Student  2. Alumni  3. Admin (University Administration)
Add a "Demo Role Switcher" (floating button) so reviewers can instantly switch between Student, Alumni and Admin without logging in again.

=== 5. PAGES TO BUILD ===

A. PUBLIC PAGES
1. Landing Page: hero section with headline, tagline, CTA buttons (Login / Register); problem vs solution section; 4 feature cards (Verified Directory, Mentorship, Direct Chat, Admin Desk); live stats counters (Alumni, Students, Companies, Mentorship Sessions); "How it works" in 3 steps; featured alumni carousel; footer with BAUST info.
2. Login Page: email/university ID and password, role selection.
3. Registration Page: multi-step form. Step 1: role (Student or Alumni). Step 2: BAUST ID, department, batch, passing year. Step 3: upload ID card or document for verification. Step 4: success screen saying "Your profile is pending admin verification".

B. STUDENT PAGES
4. Student Dashboard: welcome banner, quick stats, recommended alumni, upcoming mentorship sessions, recent messages, career resources.
5. Alumni Directory (Search and Filter): search bar plus filters for Job Sector (Government, Private, Abroad, Research, Business), Company, Batch, Department, Location. Alumni cards with photo, name, verified badge, designation, company, batch, "View Profile" and "Message" buttons. Grid/list toggle and pagination.
6. Alumni Profile Page: verified badge, bio, current job, work experience timeline, education, skills, achievements, contact/connect button, "Request Mentorship" button, available session slots.
7. Mentorship Module: tabs for Find Mentor, My Requests, Upcoming Sessions, Past Sessions. Request modal (topic: CV Review / Interview Prep / Higher Studies / Career Guidance). Online session cards with date, time and meeting-link button.
8. In-App Chat: WhatsApp/Messenger-style UI with conversation list, message thread, typing indicator, attachment button (for CV), online status.
9. My Profile and Settings (edit profile, skills, CV upload, privacy settings).

C. ALUMNI PAGES
10. Alumni Dashboard: profile completion progress, mentorship requests received (accept/decline), upcoming sessions, impact stats (students mentored), recent service requests.
11. University Admin Desk (service requests): form to request Transcript, Certificate, Testimonial, Others (document type, copies, delivery method, purpose, payment info mockup). "My Requests" table with a tracking timeline (Submitted → Under Review → Approved → Ready/Delivered) and status badges.
12. Alumni Mentor Settings: set available time slots, topics, and mentoring on/off toggle.

D. ADMIN PAGES
13. Admin Dashboard: analytics cards plus charts (registrations over time, alumni by job sector as a pie chart, alumni by batch as a bar chart, requests by status).
14. Verification Queue: table of pending registrations with preview of uploaded document, Approve / Reject (with reason) actions.
15. User Management: list of all alumni and students with search, filter, block/unblock.
16. Service Request Management: table of alumni requests, change status, add remarks, and a detail drawer.
17. Announcements: create and publish notices/events visible to all users.

E. COMMON FEATURES
- Notification bell with dropdown (mentorship accepted, request status updated, new message).
- Global 404 page and a protected-route structure per role.
- Toast notifications for all actions.

=== 6. MOCK DATA ===
Create at least 20 realistic alumni (Bangladeshi names; departments like CSE, EEE, Civil, Textile, BBA; companies such as Grameenphone, Brain Station 23, BJIT, Samsung R&D, bKash, Government cadre, Universities abroad; batches 2015-2024), 10 students, 15 service requests with mixed statuses, 10 mentorship sessions, and chat conversations. Use placeholder avatars (e.g. https://i.pravatar.cc or initials avatars).

=== 7. CODE ARCHITECTURE (VERY IMPORTANT) ===
Three teammates will later "remix" this project and each will add or upgrade separate features. So the code MUST be modular and conflict-free:
- Folder structure: /src/components (shared UI), /src/pages/{public,student,alumni,admin}, /src/layouts, /src/data, /src/hooks, /src/routes, /src/utils, /src/types.
- One page = one file. Reusable components (Button, Card, Badge, Modal, Table, Input, Avatar, Sidebar, Navbar, StatCard, Toast) built once in /src/components/ui.
- Centralized route config in /src/routes and a central theme/design-token config so global styling changes are easy.
- Clean comments marking where backend/API integration will happen later (e.g. "// TODO: replace with API call").
- No placeholder "coming soon" pages: every listed page must be fully designed and functional with mock data.

=== 8. OUTPUT EXPECTATION ===
Generate the complete working app with all pages above, polished enough to present to a university faculty panel. After the code, give a short summary of the page list and routes.








